summary:
  The line that clears away older address files takes the files with a later
  start time in their name, not an earlier one.

history:
  Each recording's write first removes the address files of recordings
  started before it, so that one left by a write landing after its own
  cleanup does not stay. The line can itself run late, after the next
  recording has written its file. Which files are older is therefore read
  from the names: a late line must take nothing that was started after it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RecLogic.js

find:
      return "for f in " + quotedPrefix + "*; do t=${f##*.}; [ \"$t\" -lt " + beforeMs

replace:
      return "for f in " + quotedPrefix + "*; do t=${f##*.}; [ \"$t\" -gt " + beforeMs

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_reclogic.qml::test_older_files_are_taken_by_the_time_in_their_name
  and tests/test_recording_stop_race.py::test_a_late_write_of_the_recording_before_changes_no_station.
  Line-neutral.
